 "drivingQuestion": "Is the oven measure grain or bread; and if bread, which arrangement?",
 "outcome": "teiku",
 "outcomeNote": "First dilemma resolved (bread); the follow-up dilemma stands as teiku.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": "taanit.sugya089",
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "taanit.22b.8",
   "daf": "22b",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "תָּא שְׁמַע: כִּמְלֹא פִי תַנּוּר. וַעֲדַיִין תִּיבְּעֵי לְהוּ: כְּכִיסּוּיָא דְתַנּוּרָא, אוֹ דִלְמָא כִּי דָרָא דְרִיפְתָּא דְּהָדַר לֵיהּ לְפוּמָּא דְתַנּוּרָא? תֵּיקוּ.",
   "en": "The Gemara answers: «Come» and «hear» the phrase of the mishna: Enough «to fill the mouth of an oven.» This indicates that the bread referred to does not fill the entire oven, but rather covers the mouth of the oven. The Gemara further asks: «And still you can raise this dilemma before them:» Is the mishna referring to the bread «of the cover of the oven? Perhaps» it is referring «to a row of bread around the mouth of the oven.» No resolution was found, and the Gemara states that the dilemma «shall stand» unresolved."
  }
 ],
